# Test/CI environment template — safe to commit. NOT SECRETS.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-09-23. `env_config.load_env()` requires three variables and raises
# `RuntimeError` when any is missing. They normally come from
# `backend/.env`, which is **gitignored** — so it exists on a developer
# machine and not in a fresh checkout, which is exactly the shape that made
# `tests/unit/test_agent_persist.py::test_cli_passes_tasks_file_through`
# fail on CI while passing locally (found by staircase shard u-55, run
# 35852698516; that shard was the first one to reach the test at all, because
# the full `unit` shard wedges before it gets there).
#
# Every value below is a placeholder whose only job is to satisfy the
# loader. Real credentials must never be added here — this file is tracked,
# and a committed key is a leak that a `git rm` does not undo. A developer's
# own `backend/.env` always wins: `tests/conftest.py` only materialises this
# template when `backend/.env` is absent.
#
# `env_config.REQUIRED_VARS` is the authority for what must appear here:
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, NOTION_TOKEN, NOTION_PARENT_PAGE_ID
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY must keep the `sk-ant-` prefix: `env_config.validate_config`
# rejects anything else, and that check is worth keeping honest.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-ci-placeholder-not-a-real-key

NOTION_TOKEN=ci-placeholder-not-a-real-token
NOTION_PARENT_PAGE_ID=ci-placeholder-not-a-real-page-id

TIMEZONE=UTC
